{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he turned and went down.</b> One needs to know why it says <b>and he turned</b>, for it is not the way of proper conduct that Moshe should turn away; perhaps it is for this reason that Scripture was precise in saying <b>from the mountain</b>, so as not to say that, heaven forbid, he behaved with a lack of proper conduct by turning his back toward the Shekhinah — rather it was from the mountain that he turned. Yet it is difficult: if so, it should have said ״וַיִּפֶן מִן הָהָר״. And further it is difficult that there was no need to say ״וַיִּפֶן״ at all." "Or perhaps it intends to say that his strength failed, and he was afraid of the angels, and he would make way for himself to the sides of the mountain like a person hiding while walking." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend according to what they said (Devarim Rabbah 1): to what is Moshe's way compared? When he would speak with HaKadosh Barukh Hu he would say ״לָמָּה ה׳ יֶחֱרֶה״ etc., and when he went to Israel he reversed the order and said ״אַתֶּם חֲטָאתֶם״ etc. — and this is the meaning of <b>and he turned</b>: that the original set of features he would display when standing before the Place was no longer maintained." "<b>The tablets of the testimony.</b> Or perhaps it also alluded, in saying <b>the testimony</b>, that they testify that they are written with the writing of Elohim, inasmuch as their script is wondrous on this side and that side equally — something that this script cannot be through human craft, for the letter changes its shape from the other side. Also the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Megillah 3a) who said that the mem and samekh in the tablets stood miraculously — or perhaps this sign combines with the sign of the making of the tablets, and the two signs constitute testimony, since testimony requires no less than two. And this is what it says: <b>and the tablets were the work of Elohim</b> — here is one witness; <b>and the writing was the writing of Elohim</b> — a second witness."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:04.694817363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}